      "writtenOn": "2025-04-09T15:05:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree with that. However, due to the backwards compatibility, i.e. supporting HTTP-Passwords, some places need to evict entries from the token cache, when External IDs are modified. Thus, until the HTTP password support is fully removed, we need to have multiple implementations.\nAnother issue is, that Google uses a different account storage. Thus, we have to provide them with an overall Noop solution.",
